          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पारितोषिकम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पारितोषिकम् — pāritoṣikam — \"a prize\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pāritoṣika comes from paritoṣa, \"delight, satisfaction\", built on pari- and the root √tuṣ, \"to be pleased\" (MW). It first meant \"gratifying\", and then \"a reward\", the thing that pleases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
