              "text": "nimantraṇa is built on ni- and mantrayate, \"speaks, takes counsel\", a verb MW makes from mantra, which is built on the root √man, \"to think\". MW glosses it \"invitation, a summons\", and Hindi took it over as nimantraṇ."
