              "text": "sabhā is of unknown derivation, MW says, though probably connected with sa-, \"together\". MW compares Gothic sibja, \"kinship\", and English gossip, which MW also cites in its older form god-sib. It is a Rigvedic word for an assembly or hall (CDIAL 13167)."
