              "text": "goṣṭhī comes from goṣṭha, a cow-pen, built on go, \"cow\", and stha, \"standing\" (MW). The cow-pen became a meeting place, then an assembly, then a talk (CDIAL 4339). Marathi goṭh now means \"a tale\"."
